C([143], 'L2', 'Task 4 on Monad (L-1251): where Monad\'s execution at tag v0.16.7 clears transient storage between the transactions of a block.',
  'Each transaction runs in a new State object over the block state, on the first attempt and on the retry after a failed merge (category/execution/ethereum/execute_transaction.cpp lines 458 and 484). Transient values live in AccountState::transient_storage_ (state3/account_state.hpp lines 70, 126-133, 151-154), which State builds from block_state_.read_account. That call returns only the account (state3/state.cpp lines 51-59, state2/block_state.cpp lines 58-77). BlockState::merge copies the account and storage_ of each touched address and never transient_storage_ (state2/block_state.cpp lines 194-235). A transaction therefore starts with empty transient storage, and CURRENCY_SLOT and RESERVES_OF_SLOT (src/libraries/CurrencyReserves.sol:11-13) read zero there. This is what EIP-1153 requires. The Monad endpoints rpc.monad.xyz and rpc-mainnet.monadinfra.com (Monad/0.16.7) do not serve eth_simulateV1, and rpc2.monad.xyz (an erpc proxy) refuses it, so the live test did not run on Monad.',
  'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/category-labs/monad/v0.16.7/category/execution/ethereum/execute_transaction.cpp ; https://raw.githubusercontent.com/category-labs/monad/v0.16.7/category/execution/ethereum/state3/account_state.hpp ; https://raw.githubusercontent.com/category-labs/monad/v0.16.7/category/execution/ethereum/state3/state.cpp ; https://raw.githubusercontent.com/category-labs/monad/v0.16.7/category/execution/ethereum/state2/block_state.cpp ; https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ethereum/EIPs/master/EIPS/eip-1153.md')
